  "open_class": {
    "policy": "Lexical relation heads the prompt licenses generically rather than enumerating: kind-level relations, symmetric/reciprocal relations, nominalization relations. They cannot be checked by name — the validator checks position and arity only. Never frozen: these are the primary consolidation targets. Obliques are ALSO open class: prompt.txt attaches an oblique under a head named after its own preposition/adverb, so the head set cannot be enumerated in advance. `oblique_prepositions` lists the English prepositions that may therefore appear as an arity-2 head; an UpperCamelCase head that is NOT one of them is still flagged.",
    "positions": [
      "head of a kind-level relation atom, e.g. (Carry mosquito malaria)",
      "head of a symmetric relation atom accompanied by (Symmetric <head>)",
      "head of a nominalization kind-relation, e.g. (Build dam_builder dam)",
      "skolem-function head (sk_<verb>) in a scope construction, e.g. (sk_y $x)"
    ]
  }
